senses.gloss:
पतत्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, winged, feathered, flying;
(Ved.) an epithet of a particular form of fire, of the
vehicle of the Aśvins, &c.; (ई), m. a bird; a horse;
the horse in the Aśva-medha sacrifice (Rāmāyaṇa I.
13); an arrow; (इणी), n. du., Ved. day and night;
[cf. पातत्रिण.]

पतेर, अस्, आ, अम्, flying, falling; going, moving;
(अस्), m. a bird; a hole, pit; a particular measure
(= आढक).

1. पात्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see p. 564, col. 1),
to be felled, to be caused to fall, to be precipitated;
to be inflicted or imposed (as a penalty).

पत्तङ्ग पत्तङ्ग, अस्, अम्, m. n. (probably
a corruption of पत्त्राङ्ग), red sandal or sanders;
(अम्), n. Cæsalpina Sappan.

2. पातृ, ता, त्री, तृ (for 1. see p. 559, col. 3),
a defender, protector, defending (with gen. or acc.);
(ता), m. a species of Ocymum (= गन्ध-पत्त्र).
